{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting. The current code state: `DeployRickCustomizations` currently does NOT deploy think/research/exporter agents. The comment says \"think/research/exporter agent frontmatter 不在此落盘（task9 经职责 3 写入 AgentDir()/agents/）\". So task9 is supposed to implement that.\n\n`requiredRickAgents` is empty; task9 should set it to `[\"think.md\", \"research.md\", \"exporter.md\"]` presumably, or maybe just `[\"think\", \"research\", \"exporter\"]`. Note `CheckRickAgents` checks `filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"agents\", name)` where name includes extension? Currently the check appends name directly, so if requiredRickAgents = []string{\"think.md\"} then it checks `agents/think.md`. That aligns.\n\nLet me look at the env_test.go to understand the existing test patterns, and understand how the tests are structured. Also check the `settings.go` for how `AgentDir` usage works, and look at how the `DeployRickCustomizations` is invoked (init-pi command).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Wgk0OSPWUZlzWufSnjtw2946","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/env/env_test.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2430,"output":299,"cacheRead":17792,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":237,"totalTokens":20521,"cost":{"input":0.0010570500000000001,"output":0.00026013,"cacheRead":0.000064496,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0013816760000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786907703276,"responseId":"9ce453ae-a41d-4c49-b268-bdd6262dd1ad","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
