keywords present in the source. This strengthens the \"wiki 内容注入成功\" assertion beyond just non-empty. Good idea — matches \"异常（system prompt 非空）... 预期 = ≥1（wiki 内容注入成功）\". The intent is \"wiki content injected\", so checking a wiki-specific keyword is appropriate. But I must be careful: if the implementation strips the leading `# skill:...` line or not. The keywords \"尽调树\", \"信源加权\", \"大纲\", \"RFC\", \"推理识别\", \"启发性\" all appear in the body of the source files (not just the title line). Let me verify:\n- think.md: \"推理识别\" appears in \"### 1. 推理过程识别\" and \"启发性\" appears in title and \"3 启发性问题\". Body definitely contains them.\n- research.md: \"尽调树\" appears many times, \"信源加权\" appears.\n- exporter.md: \"大纲\" appears, \"RFC\" appears.\n\nGood. These keywords are robust.\n\nBut wait — I should be careful about over-asserting. The spec's exception test only says \"frontmatter 闭合后存在非空正文\". Adding keyword checks is a reasonable strengthening aligned with \"wiki 内容注入成功\". I'll include them but keep them as separate clear error messages so failures are diagnosable. Actually, if the implementation's system prompt content differs slightly, keyword checks could cause false failures. But the task explicitly says system prompt = the wiki content of `templates/skills/*.md`. So keywords must be present. I'll include them.\n\nHmm, but there's a risk: the implementation might use the OLD template content from `internal/prompt/templates/think.md` (not `templates/skills/think.md`)? Wait, the task says \"system prompt = `templates/skills/think.md`\". And the manager.go has BOTH:\n- `//go:embed templates/think.md` → thinkTemplate (a separate template, likely the old prompt)\n- `//go:embed templates/skills` → skillsFS\n\nThe task explicitly says system prompt = `templates/skills/think.md` (the skill file). So the content should be from `templates/skills/think.md`. I read that file earlier and it contains \"推理识别\", \"启发性\", \"4 维打分\", etc. Good.\n\nLet me verify the `templates/think.md` (non-skills) to distinguish, in case there's ambiguity.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_TPV2DFfDU6dkEL9W7PlS4891","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== templates/think.md (head) ===\" && head -30 internal/prompt/templates/think.md && echo \"...\" && echo \"=== templates/research.md (head) ===\" && head -20 internal/prompt/templates/research.md && echo \"=== templates/exporter.md (head) ===\" && head -20 internal/prompt/templates/exporter.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":169,"output":3351,"cacheRead":71552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3214,"totalTokens":75072,"cost":{"input":0.000073515,"output":0.00291537,"cacheRead":0.000259376,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003248261}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786907958961,"responseId":"b22853a5-3f00-4413-9a98-47985b679895","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_TPV2DFfDU6dkEL9W7PlS4891","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== templates/think.md (head) ===\n# think subagent\n\n草稿：{{draft_dir}} | rfc：{{rfc_dir}} | 本次会话：{{loop_dir}}\n\n**先读**：`{{think_skill_path}}`\n\n---\n\n## 角色\n\nthink = 推理过程分析师 + 风险评估师。**输入 = 现状+预期**(sense_loop 派发时携带),**输出 = top-N 假设清单 + 每假设 3 启发性问题**(信念/前提/反例)。\n\n不替 human 决策假设是否成立,只输出待判断假设及风险评估。\n\n---\n\n## 工作流(6 步)\n\n| 步骤 | 动作 |\n|---|---|\n| 1. 推理识别 | 从\"现状+预期\"标注演绎/归纳/溯因推理段 |\n| 2. 假设提取 | 按推理类型分流提取隐含假设(模板见 skill) |\n| 3. 假设数量保障 | 至少 {{min_assumptions}} 个,低于则补强(见下方专节) |\n| 4. 形式化 + 3 启发性问题 | 写成\"如果 X 那么 Y\"形式,每假设生成 3 问(信念/前提/反例) |\n| 5. 4 维打分 | 影响范围 / 不可逆性 / 影响程度 / 置信度 |\n| 6. 期望值 + top-N | 计算最终分,选 top-N |\n\n---\n\n## 推理类型识别\n...\n=== templates/research.md (head) ===\n# research subagent\n\n草稿：{{draft_dir}} | rfc：{{rfc_dir}} | 本次会话：{{loop_dir}}\n\n**先读**：`{{research_skill_path}}`\n\n---\n\n## 角色\n\nresearch = main agent + 调度器。**不直接调研**,只维护尽调树、配置信源、派发 subagent、整合报告。\n\n3 个概念:\n1. **尽调树**:每层 MECE 划分(不重复不遗漏),节点产生疑问则下钻\n2. **信源加权**:置信度 = Σ(信源验证结果 × 权重)\n3. **subagent 上下文隔离**:具体调研派给 subagent 落盘\n\n**终止条件**:所有叶节点置信度 = 高(≥ 0.8)。无法达高的叶节点附理由 R7 上报。\n\n---\n=== templates/exporter.md (head) ===\n# exporter subagent\n\n草稿：{{draft_dir}} | rfc：{{rfc_dir}} | 本次会话：{{loop_dir}}\n\n**先读**：`{{exporter_skill_path}}`\n\n---\n\n## 角色\n\n接收 sense_loop 派发的 RFC 输出任务，按**大纲+内容两阶段**执行：先向 human 确认大纲，确认后再填内容。\n\n每次调用只处理一次输出任务。产出是 RFC 文件。\n\n---\n\n## 工作流\n\n```\n1. 读「先读」行指定的 skill 方法论\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786907999525},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both `templates/think.md` (the subagent prompt template) and `templates/skills/think.md` (the skill) contain \"启发性\", \"4 维\", \"推理识别\". So keyword checks can't fully distinguish. But the task explicitly says system prompt = `templates/skills/think.md` (the skill wiki content). The skill wiki content has the `# skill:think(...)` heading and the specific methodology. The `templates/think.md` (subagent prompt) has `# think subagent` heading and `{{...}}` placeholders.\n\nKey distinguishing markers for the SKILL content (templates/skills/*.md):\n- think.md skill: starts with `# skill:think(推理过程分析+4 维风险评估+启发性 3 问方法论)`\n- research.md skill: starts with `# skill:research（尽调树+信源加权方法论）`\n- exporter.md skill: starts with `# skill:exporter（RFC 输出方法论）`\n\nSo a strong check: the body contains `skill:think`, `skill:research`, `skill:exporter` respectively. Or check for the \"skill:\" prefix which appears only in the skill files, not the subagent templates.\n\nActually, even simpler and more robust: the skill files have `# skill:think` etc. in the first line (which becomes the body, since frontmatter is before it). So I can assert body contains `skill:think` (think), `skill:research` (research), `skill:exporter` (exporter). This uniquely identifies the skill wiki content vs the subagent template.\n\nBut wait — is the system prompt body going to include the `# skill:...` heading? The implementation will read the skill file content (via `LoadCoreSkills` → `skillsFS.ReadFile(\"templates/skills/think.md\")`) which returns the ENTIRE file including `# skill:think(...)` heading. So the body will start with `# skill:think(...)`. \n\nHowever, there's a subtlety: the implementation might strip the leading `# skill:...` line or not. To be safe, I'll check for the keyword markers that are unambiguous:\n- `skill:think` (only in skills/think.md, not in templates/think.md)\n- `skill:research` (only in skills/research.md)\n- `skill:exporter` (only in skills/exporter.md)\n\nLet me verify `templates/think.md` does NOT contain \"skill:think\". From the head output, it contains `# think subagent` and `{{think_skill_path}}` — no \"skill:think\". Good. `templates/research.md` has `{{research_skill_path}}` — no \"skill:research\". Good. `templates/exporter.md` has `{{exporter_skill_path}}` — no \"skill:exporter\". Good.\n\nSo my body content checks:\n- think.md body contains `skill:think`\n- research.md body contains `skill:research`\n- exporter.md body contains `skill:exporter`\n\nPlus the generic non-empty check (≥1 non-blank line), which is subsumed by the keyword check but I'll keep the explicit non-empty check per the test method's awk equivalence.\n\nActually, I'll do both: (a) non-empty body (≥1 non-blank line) per the test method, and (b) contains the skill-specific marker. Both are clear.\n\nNow, let me also reconsider the \"real agent discovery entry\" check. I'll verify by parsing frontmatter names. This is the \"等价机制\". I could optionally also try `pi` binary if available to truly list agents, but that's risky. Let me check if there's a simple non-interactive way... Actually pi is a TUI that needs a terminal. Running `pi --help` might show subcommands. Let me check quickly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_yMfuYQcVs97UK2G2Pxdx1915","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && timeout 20 /home/hadoop-recsys/.local/bin/pi --help 2>&1 | head -50; echo \"exit=$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":721,"output":922,"cacheRead":75008,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":832,"totalTokens":76651,"cost":{"input":0.000313635,"output":0.00080214,"cacheRead":0.000271904,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0013876790000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786907999526,"responseId":"b8ed5dfe-377a-453f-a6b3-513ed4508f2d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_yMfuYQcVs97UK2G2Pxdx1915","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"pi - AI coding assistant with read, bash, edit, write tools\n\nUsage:\n  pi [options] [@files...] [messages...]\n\nCommands:\n  pi install <source> [-l]     Install extension source and add to settings\n  pi remove <source> [-l]      Remove extension source from settings\n  pi uninstall <source> [-l]   Alias for remove\n  pi update [source|self|pi]   Update pi, extensions, or model catalogs\n  pi list                      List installed extensions from settings\n  pi config [-l]               Open TUI to enable/disable package resources (Tab switches scope)\n  pi auth <command>            Print credentials or check provider readiness\n  pi <command> --help          Show help for install/remove/uninstall/update/list/config/auth\n\nOptions:\n  --provider <name>              Provider name (default: google)\n  --model <pattern>              Model pattern or ID (supports \"provider/id\" and optional \":<thinking>\")\n  --api-key <key>                API key (defaults to env vars)\n  --system-prompt <text>         System prompt (default: coding assistant prompt)\n  --append-system-prompt <text>  Append text or file contents to the system prompt (can be used multiple times)\n  --mode <mode>                  Output mode: text (default), json, or rpc\n  --print, -p                    Non-interactive mode: process prompt and exit\n  --continue, -c                 Continue previous session\n  --resume, -r                   Select a session to resume\n  --session <path|id>            Use specific session file or partial UUID\n  --session-id <id>              Use exact project session ID, creating it if missing\n  --fork <path|id>               Fork specific session file or partial UUID into a new session\n  --session-dir <dir>            Directory for session storage and lookup\n  --no-session                   Don't save session (ephemeral)\n  --name, -n <name>              Set session display name\n  --models <patterns>            Comma-separated model patterns for Ctrl+P cycling\n                                 Supports globs (anthropic/*, *sonnet*) and fuzzy matching\n  --no-tools, -nt                Disable all tools by default (built-in and extension)\n  --no-builtin-tools, -nbt       Disable built-in tools by default but keep extension/custom tools enabled\n  --tools, -t <tools>            Comma-separated allowlist of tool names to enable\n                                 Applies to built-in, extension, and custom tools\n  --exclude-tools, -xt <tools>   Comma-separated denylist of tool names to disable\n                                 Applies to built-in, extension, and custom tools\n  --thinking <level>             Set thinking level: off, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max\n  --extension, -e <path>         Load an extension file (can be used multiple times)\n  --no-extensions, -ne           Disable extension discovery (explicit -e paths still work)\n  --skill <path>                 Load a skill file or directory (can be used multiple times)\n  --no-skills, -ns               Disable skills discovery and loading\n  --prompt-template <path>       Load a prompt template file or directory (can be used multiple times)\n  --no-prompt-templates, -np     Disable prompt template discovery and loading\n  --theme <path>                 Load a theme file or directory (can be used multiple times)\n  --no-themes                    Disable theme discovery and loading\n  --no-context-files, -nc        Disable AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md discovery and loading\n  --export <file>                Export session file to HTML and exit\nexit=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786908015312},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's `pi --print -p` (non-interactive mode: process prompt and exit) and `--mode rpc`. The pi binary supports non-interactive mode. Could I use it to run `{action:\"list\"}`? The subagent tool is a builtin/extension tool. Running `pi -p \"list agents\" --mode json` might invoke the model... but that requires an API key and a model. Too heavy and unreliable.\n\nActually, wait — the subagent tool with `{action:\"list\"}` is a tool the LLM calls, not a CLI. There's no direct CLI to list agents. The research-report says `{action:\"list\"}` is the discovery entry via the subagent tool.\n\nGiven the test environment constraints, I'll use the \"equivalent mechanism\": verify agent files in the discovery directory with correct frontmatter names. This is the same data source pi's `{action:\"list\"}` reads (agent file discovery in `agents/**/*.md`). I'll document this in the script's docstring as the equivalent.\n\nNow, let me also verify: does the pi-subagents agent discovery actually read from `~/.pi/agent/agents/**/*.md` (user scope) → mapped to `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR/agents/**/*.md`? From research-report B2: \"User = `~/.pi/agent/agents/**/*.md`\". And rick's isolated mapping: \"user 级 = `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/**/*.md`\". So `$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/agents/*.md` is correct.\n\nNow let me finalize the frontmatter expectations. What exactly will the `defaultContext` value be? The task says \"frontmatter 含 name/description/tools/defaultContext\". It doesn't specify value. I'll just check presence of the key.\n\nNow, an important consideration: should I check `description` is non-empty? The task says frontmatter contains `description`. I'll check presence and non-empty (since a description field with empty value would be useless). I'll check presence; optionally non-empty. Let me check presence + non-empty for description (to be meaningful).\n\nLet me also reconsider: the `tools` field. For think, task says `tools: read, grep, find, ls`. For research: `read, grep, find, ls, bash, web_search, fetch_content`. For exporter: `read, write, bash`. I'll assert exact match (normalizing whitespace/commas). I'll compare the normalized sorted list of tools.\n\nLet me normalize: split `fm['tools']` by comma, strip, sort → compare to sorted expected list. This is robust to ordering differences. But actually the task lists them in a specific order. I could check exact string too. To be safe against minor ordering, I'll compare as sorted sets. But then if the implementation has wrong tools (missing one), sorted-set comparison catches it. Good.\n\nActually, let me compare both: exact set equality via sorted lists, and also that the count matches. Sorted list equality covers both.\n\nNow let me also think: should the test script also check the Go source for `requiredRickAgents` being updated (i.e., CheckRickAgents lists the 3 agents)? The task goal doesn't explicitly require `requiredRickAgents` to change; key result 3 says \"验收断言用真实入口\". But the `CheckRickAgents` function currently has empty `requiredRickAgents`. Task9 might or might not update it. The task goal says \"此任务产出的是 env 职责 3（DeployRickCustomizations）中「agent」定制物的具体内容\" — focused on deployment, not the check. But key result 3 mentions discovery. The `CheckRickAgents` is职责4 (check), not 职责3. \n\nThe test method (the authoritative spec for my test) only mentions:\n1. Normal: 3 files exist + head -5 + discovery lists 3 names.\n2. Boundary: idempotent + overwrite.\n3. Exception: system prompt non-empty.\n\nSo I should focus on these. I could optionally add a structural source check that the deployment function exists and references the 3 agents, but the test method doesn't require it. I'll keep to the