= doing\n2. dirname(doing) = job_35\n3. dirname(job_35) = jobs\n4. dirname(jobs) = .rick\n5. dirname(.rick) = repo_root ✓\n\nBut since `.git` is at repo_root, the `.git` probe will find it first. Good.\n\nNow let me write the script with all phases. I'll also add cleanup of temp dirs at the end (optional, but good hygiene). Actually temp dirs under /tmp are fine; I'll clean the Go program dir and build dirs.\n\nLet me carefully write parse_frontmatter to handle the closing `---` correctly. The frontmatter closes with a line that is exactly `---`. The system prompt body might also contain `---`? Looking at the skill files: think.md has `---` separator lines? Let me check. The skill files (templates/skills/think.md) — do they contain `---` lines? \n\nFrom my read of think.md (skill), I see `---` separators? Let me check: The skill file starts with `# skill:think(...)` then a paragraph, then `---`, then `## think pipeline`. Yes! The skill files contain `---` lines in the BODY (as markdown horizontal rules). So my frontmatter parser must only treat the SECOND `---` line as the closing delimiter (i.e., the first `---` after the opening `---`).\n\nMy parse_frontmatter finds the first line equal to `---` after index 0. Since frontmatter fields are `name:`, `description:`, etc. (no `---` among them), the first `---` after opening is the closing delimiter. Good. The body then contains subsequent `---` lines (markdown rules), but I don't care about those for parsing; I just take body = everything after the closing delimiter.\n\nBut wait — what if the description field's value is multi-line (YAML block) and contains `---`? Unlikely for this task; description will be a single line. I'll assume single-line frontmatter values.\n\nLet me verify the skill files don't have `---` immediately as line 1. The skill files start with `# skill:...`, not `---`. So the agent file = frontmatter (`---` + fields + `---`) + body (which starts with `# skill:...`). Good.\n\nNow, the awk in the test method: `awk '/^---$/{n++} n>=2 && /[^[:space:]]/{print}'`. This increments n on each `---` line and prints non-blank lines when n>=2 (i.e., after the 2nd `---`). This matches my body extraction (after 2nd `---`). Note: awk's `/^---$/` matches exactly `---` lines. My body extraction splits at the line that strips to `---`. Equivalent enough.\n\nLet me write a helper `count_body_nonblank_lines` equivalent to the awk+grep -c, returning count.\n\nNow let me also double check: the `head -5` check. `head -5 think.md` gives first 5 lines. Frontmatter:\n```\n---\nname: think\ndescription: ...\ntools: read, grep, find, ls\ndefaultContext: ...\n```\nSo lines: `---`, `name: think`, `description: ...`, `tools: ...`, `defaultContext: ...`. `name: think` is line 2, within first 5. Good.\n\nNow, let me write the script.\n\nI need to decide on the expected tools as sorted lists:\n- think: ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls']\n- research: ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls', 'bash', 'web_search', 'fetch_content']\n- exporter: ['read', 'write', 'bash']\n\nI'll store as list and compare sorted.\n\nNow let me write.\n\nActually, also consider: `web_search` and `fetch_content` — these are the actual pi tool names? The task says \"tools 声明对齐 pi 工具名\". In the subagent tool schema, tools include `read`, `bash`, `grep`, `find`, `ls`, `edit`, `write`, `web_search`, `fetch_content`, etc. So `web_search` and `fetch_content` are correct pi tool names. Good.\n\nNow write the file.\n\nLet me also think about whether to verify `defaultContext` non-empty. I'll check presence and non-empty. The value is typically `fresh` or `fork`. I won't assert a specific value.\n\nLet me write the complete script now.\n\nFor the overwrite semantics test, I need to pre-place a file at `agent_dir/agents/think.md` BEFORE running deploy. The deploy should skip overwriting it (because no `rick-managed: true`). But note: if the file has no frontmatter at all (just \"user custom content\"), the overwrite check \"file frontmatter contains rick-managed: true\" would be false → skip. Good. Let me pre-place content without `rick-managed`:\n```\n---\nname: think\ndescription: user custom agent\n---\nuser custom body\n```\nNo `rick-managed: true`. After deploy, this file should be unchanged.\n\nBut wait — will the implementation's overwrite logic check for `rick-managed: true` anywhere in the file, or specifically in frontmatter? The task says \"覆盖判定 = 文件 frontmatter 含 rick 固定标记（如 rick-managed: true）才覆盖\". So frontmatter must contain `rick-managed: true`. My unmarked file has frontmatter WITHOUT that marker. Good.\n\nFor the marked overwrite test, pre-place:\n```\n---\nname: research\ndescription: stale rick agent\ntools: read\ndefaultContext: fresh\nrick-managed: true\n---\nSTALE BODY\n```\nAfter deploy, this should be overwritten (content changes to fresh system prompt with `skill:research`). Assert: after deploy, research.md no longer contains \"STALE BODY\" and contains \"skill:research\" and \"rick-managed: true\".\n\nLet me now also handle: in the marked overwrite test, I pre-place only research.md (marked stale). After deploy, think.md and exporter.md should be freshly created too. I'll just assert research.md got overwritten.\n\nNow, one more consideration for the overwrite tests: they need a fresh `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR` per phase, and fresh HOME. I'll create fresh temp dirs.\n\nLet me write a helper to pre-create the agents dir:\n```python\ndef preplace(path, content):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(content)\n```\n\nNow let me assemble everything.\n\nLet me also decide: should I run `go test ./internal/env/...` as part of the test? The test method doesn't require it, but task3/task5 tests run go test to verify Go unit tests pass. For task9, the implementation will add Go unit tests. Running `go test ./internal/env/...` would verify those. But my Python test's core is behavioral via the temp Go program. Adding `go test ./internal/env/...` would also catch compilation issues. I think it's reasonable to add a `go build ./cmd/rick` + `go test ./internal/env/...` as a light structural/compilation check, since task9 modifies internal/env. This matches the pattern in task3.py. Let me add:\n- `go build ./cmd/rick` (verify the whole thing compiles with new env code) — optional but good.\n- Actually, the temp Go program already compiles internal/env. But a full `go test ./internal/env/...` verifies the env package tests (which task9 will add). I'll include `go test ./internal/env/...`.\n\nBut careful: `go test ./internal/env/...` currently passes (existing tests). After task9 implementation, there will be more tests. Running it now (RED phase) — the existing tests pass, so `go test` won't fail. That's fine; it's not the primary RED assertion. My behavioral deploy assertions are the RED part.\n\nActually, I want to keep the test focused and not add noise. But including `go test ./internal/env/...` is consistent with the task's reference skills and other task tests, and it verifies the implementation compiles + unit tests pass. I'll include it but keep it as a secondary check (errors appended, not blocking other checks).\n\nLet me include:\n1. `go test -timeout 120s ./internal/env/...` — verifies env package compiles and its tests pass.\n\nThis is lightweight and valuable. I'll add it near the end.\n\nNow, let me write the script.\n\nActually, I realize I should double-check one thing: when I run `go run .` in the temp dir, the Go program's cwd is the temp dir (dot-prefixed under repo_root). `workspace.GetRickDir()` returns `<tempdir>/.rick` which doesn't exist → `deployRickCustomizations` reads `os.ReadDir(<tempdir>/.rick/skills)` → IsNotExist → returns nil. So only the agent deployment (if added to the wrapper) runs. That's actually PERFECT isolation — it means the skills/gates copy is a no-op, and only agent deployment happens. \n\nBut wait — will task9's implementation put agent deployment in the wrapper `DeployRickCustomizations()` (after `deployRickCustomizations`) or inside `deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)`? \n\nIf it's in the wrapper after `deployRickCustomizations`, then running with cwd=tempdir (no .rick/skills) → `deployRickCustomizations` returns nil → agent deployment still runs. Good.\n\nIf it's inside `deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)` (the inner function), then agent deployment happens there too (after the skills copy, regardless). But the inner function reads embedded templates, so it doesn't need skillsDir content. It would still run. Good.\n\nEither way, my temp program with cwd=tempdir will exercise the agent deployment. \n\nBut there's a subtle risk: what if the implementation requires `.rick/skills` to exist to even call the agent deployment? Unlikely. The agent content is embedded.\n\nActually, to be MORE robust and match real usage (init-pi runs from repo root where .rick exists), I could run the temp program with cwd=repo_root. But then `go run .` with cwd=tempdir vs `go run <path>` with cwd=repo_root. Earlier I found `go run <path>` fails for dot-prefixed dirs. Let me use a NON-dot-prefixed temp dir name to allow `go run <path>`? Actually, non-dot-prefixed dirs under repo_root WOULD be picked up by `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` (which could break other things during the test run? No, my test run is separate). But a non-dot dir under repo_root with a main.go package would make `go test ./...` include it. That could cause issues if the repo has other tests. But my test script doesn't run `go test ./...` (only `./internal/env/...`). And I clean up the temp dir. Still, to avoid any accidental inclusion and match task5's proven pattern, I'll use dot-prefix + `go run .` with cwd=tempdir.\n\nBut then cwd for the Go program = tempdir, and skills deploy is a no-op. That's fine — the agents are what we test.\n\nHmm wait, but is there any chance the task9 implementation ties agent deployment to the skills dir existing? Let me think about the most natural implementation. Looking at the current `deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)`:\n- It copies rick-gates and skills from skillsDir.\n- For task9, the natural addition is a separate step that writes agents from embedded content. This could be:\n  a) A new function `deployRickAgents()` called from `DeployRickCustomizations()` wrapper.\n  b) Added inside `deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)` after the skills loop.\n\nBoth are plausible. In case (b), the function still runs when skillsDir doesn't exist (returns early `return nil` before reaching agent deployment!). Wait — look at current code:\n\n```go\nfunc deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir string) error {\n    // rick-gates hook 扩展\n    if err := copyDir(...); err != nil { ... }\n\n    // rick skills\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(skillsDir)\n    if err != nil {\n        if os.IsNotExist(err) {\n            return nil // 无 skills 目录 —— 无定制可部署。\n        }\n        return ...\n    }\n    for ... { copy skills }\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\nIf the implementation adds agent deployment INSIDE `deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)` AFTER the `os.ReadDir` early-return, then when skillsDir doesn't exist (cwd=tempdir), the function returns early BEFORE agent deployment → agents NOT deployed → my test would fail even after correct implementation! That would be a FALSE FAILURE.\n\nTo avoid this risk, I should run the temp Go program with cwd=repo_root so that `.rick/skills` EXISTS, ensuring `deployRickCustomizations` doesn't early-return and any code path (wrapper or inner) runs.\n\nBut with dot-prefixed dir + `go run .`, cwd=tempdir. I need a way to run `go run` such that the program's cwd=repo_root.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use a non-dot-prefixed temp dir and run `go run <path>` from cwd=repo_root. But then the dir would be picked up by `go test ./...` if I ran that (I don't). And I clean it up. Risk: if something else runs `go build ./...` concurrently? Unlikely during my test.\n\n2. Write the temp program to a temp dir OUTSIDE repo_root? No — internal imports require being in the module.\n\n3. Use the rick binary approach: build `rick` binary, run `rick tools init-pi` with cwd=repo_root and fake pi/npm. This runs the FULL Ensure flow including DeployRickCustomizations with cwd=repo_root. But heavy.\n\n4. Make the temp Go program itself chdir to a target dir before calling DeployRickCustomizations. I can pass the target cwd as an argument! The program:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n        if err := os.Chdir(os.Args[1]); err != nil { ... }\n    }\n    if err := env.DeployRickCustomizations(); err != nil { ... }\n}\n```\nThen I can run `go run .` with cwd=tempdir (for compilation) but pass repo_root as arg → program chdir to repo_root → `workspace.GetRickDir()` = repo_root/.rick (exists). \n\nThis is the cleanest: it isolates compilation (cwd=tempdir, dot-prefixed, ignored by go tooling) while controlling the runtime cwd via arg.\n\nLet me add a `cwd` argument to the temp program. I'll pass `repo_root` as the target cwd.\n\nActually, even simpler: I can pass the target dir via env var, but arg is fine.\n\nLet me design:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    target := \".\"\n    if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n        target = os.Args[1]\n    }\n    if err := os.Chdir(target); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chdir %s failed: %v\\n\", target, err)\n        os.Exit(2)\n    }\n    if err := env.DeployRickCustomizations(); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"deploy failed: %v\\n\", err)\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n    fmt.Println(\"deploy-ok\")\n}\n```\n\nAnd run: `go run . <repo_root>` with cwd=tempdir.\n\nWait, `go run . <repo_root>` — Go passes args after the package to the program. Yes: `go run . arg1 arg2` runs the program with args. Good.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: `go run .` with cwd=tempdir (dot-prefixed). Go ignores dot dirs for `./...` but `go run .` explicit works (confirmed earlier). And args after `.` go to the program. Let me verify `go run . <arg>` works.\n\nLet me test this quickly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_TFu5fmjttH8v05hpmxl23538","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && tmp=$(mktemp -d .tmp_task9_probe_XXXXXX) && cat > \"$tmp/main.go\" <<'EOF'\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\ttarget := \".\"\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\ttarget = os.Args[1]\n\t}\n\tif err := os.Chdir(target); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chdir failed: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\n\t}\n\tif err := env.DeployRickCustomizations(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"deploy failed: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(\"deploy-ok\")\n}\nEOF\nexport RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR=$(mktemp -d); export HOME=$(mktemp -d); (cd \"$tmp\" && go run . /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick); echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"agents dir:\"; ls -la \"$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/agents\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"no agents\"; echo \"extensions:\"; ls -la \"$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/extensions/rick-gates\" 2>/dev/null | head; rm -rf \"$tmp\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":940,"output":5448,"cacheRead":76544,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5082,"totalTokens":82932,"cost":{"input":0.0004089,"output":0.00473976,"cacheRead":0.000277472,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005426132}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786908015313,"responseId":"8393eb34-c450-41d4-a97e-a2ecab8ab752","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_TFu5fmjttH8v05hpmxl23538","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"go: downloading go1.25.0 (linux/amd64)\ndeploy-ok\nexit=0\nagents dir:\nno agents\nextensions:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys   31 Aug 17 03:22 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys   32 Aug 17 03:22 ..\n-rwxrwxr-x 1 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 1087 Aug 17 03:22 helper.py\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786908125657},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The temp program with chdir to repo_root works: it deployed rick-gates (extensions/rick-gates/helper.py exists), but no agents (feature not implemented). This confirms:\n1. The temp Go program correctly exercises `DeployRickCustomizations()`.\n2. RED phase: no agents deployed → my assertions will fail.\n\nNow let me write the full task9.py script.\n\nLet me carefully write it with all the pieces. I'll write a comprehensive but clean script.\n\nKey structure:\n- Module docstring\n- imports: json, os, shutil, subprocess, sys, tempfile, hashlib\n- helpers: find_repo_root, run, tail, read_text, sha256_file, parse_frontmatter, write_deploy_program, run_deploy\n- AGENTS spec dict\n- main()\n\nLet me write the AGENTS spec:\n```python\nAGENTS = {\n    'think': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:think',\n    },\n    'research': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls', 'bash', 'web_search', 'fetch_content'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:research',\n    },\n    'exporter': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'write', 'bash'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:exporter',\n    },\n}\n```\n\nThe `name` is the dict key.\n\nNow parse_frontmatter returns (fm, body, err). body includes everything after closing `---` line.\n\nLet me write the main flow.\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    errors = []\n    repo_root = find_repo_root(__file__)\n    go = shutil.which('go')\n    if not go:\n        result = {'pass': False, 'errors': ['go toolchain not found in PATH']}\n        print(json.dumps(result))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    prog_dir = write_deploy_program(repo_root)\n\n    # ---------- 正常路径 ----------\n    agent_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_agent_')\n    home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_home_')\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, agent_dir, home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (正常路径) exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        normal_ok = True\n        # 3 files exist + frontmatter checks\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('%s.md 未落盘: %s' % (name, p))\n                normal_ok = False\n                continue\n            content = read_text(p)\n            fm, body, ferr = parse_frontmatter(content)\n            if ferr:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 解析失败: %s' % (name, ferr))\n                normal_ok = False\n                continue\n            # name\n            if fm.get('name') != name:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter name=%r, want %r' % (name, fm.get('name'), name))\n            # tools\n            got_tools = sorted([t.strip() for t in fm.get('tools', '').split(',') if t.strip()])\n            want_tools = sorted(AGENTS[name]['tools'])\n            if got_tools != want_tools:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter tools=%r, want %r' % (name, got_tools, want_tools))\n            # description\n            if not fm.get('description'):\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺非空 description' % name)\n            # defaultContext\n            if not fm.get('defaultContext'):\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺非空 defaultContext' % name)\n            # rick-managed marker\n            if fm.get('rick-managed') != 'true':\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺 rick-managed: true 标记' % name)\n\n        # head -5 think.md\n        think_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', 'think.md')\n        if os.path.isfile(think_path):\n            head5 = read_first_n_lines(think_path, 5)\n            if 'name: think' not in head5:\n                errors.append(\"head -5 think.md 不含 `name: think`\")\n\n        # 真实发现入口（等价：解析 agents/ 下 frontmatter name 字段）\n        discovered = discover_agent_names(os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents'))\n        expected_names = set(AGENTS.keys())\n        if discovered != expected_names:\n            errors.append('agent 发现清单 = %s, want %s' % (sorted(discovered), sorted(expected_names)))\n```\n\nThen boundary idempotent (reuse agent_dir):\n```python\n        # ---------- 边界：幂等 ----------\n        before = {}\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if os.path.isfile(p):\n                before[name] = sha256_file(p)\n        rc2, out2, err2 = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, agent_dir, home)\n        if rc2 != 0:\n            errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (幂等重跑) exit=%d: %s' % (rc2, tail(err2 or out2)))\n        else:\n            changed = []\n            for name, digest in before.items():\n                p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n                if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                    changed.append('%s (file missing)' % name)\n                elif sha256_file(p) != digest:\n                    changed.append(name)\n            if changed:\n                errors.append('幂等重跑后文件内容变化: %s' % ', '.join(changed))\n```\n\nWait, but if `before` is empty (files weren't created in normal path), the idempotent check is vacuous. I should only run idempotent check if the 3 files exist. But since I'm inside `else` of `rc != 0`, and I've already appended errors for missing files, `before` may be partial. If `before` is empty, the loop over before.items() does nothing → no false error. That's acceptable: if normal path failed, we already reported errors. But to be clean, I'll guard: only do idempotent check if all 3 files exist. Actually simpler: compute before for existing files; if none exist, skip (don't add idempotent error). The loop naturally does nothing if before is empty. Good enough.\n\nThen overwrite semantics (fresh dirs):\n```python\n    # ---------- 边界：覆盖语义（无 rick-managed 标记不覆盖） ----------\n    ow_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_ow_')\n    ow_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_owhome_')\n    think_ow = os.path.join(ow_dir, 'agents', 'think.md')\n    user_content = '---\\nname: think\\ndescription: user custom agent\\ntools: read\\n---\\nUSER CUSTOM BODY\\n'\n    write_file(think_ow, user_content)\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, ow_dir, ow_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (覆盖语义-无标记) exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        after_content = read_text(think_ow)\n        if after_content != user_content:\n            errors.append('无 rick-managed 标记的 think.md 被覆盖（应跳过）')\n        for name in ('research', 'exporter'):\n            p = os.path.join(ow_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('覆盖语义场景下 %s.md 未落盘' % name)\n```\n\nThen marked overwrite (fresh dir):\n```python\n    # ---------- 边界：覆盖语义（有 rick-managed 标记才覆盖） ----------\n    mk_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_mk_')\n    mk_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_mkhome_')\n    research_mk = os.path.join(mk_dir, 'agents', 'research.md')\n    stale = '---\\nname: research\\ndescription: stale rick agent\\ntools: read\\ndefaultContext: fresh\\nrick-managed: true\\n---\\nSTALE BODY\\n'\n    write_file(research_mk, stale)\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, mk_dir, mk_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (覆盖语义-有标记) exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        after_content = read_text(research_mk)\n        if after_content == stale:\n            errors.append('含 rick-managed: true 的 research.md 未被覆盖（应覆盖）')\n        elif 'STALE BODY' in (after_content or ''):\n            errors.append('含 rick-managed: true 的 research.md 覆盖后仍含 STALE BODY')\n        elif 'skill:research' not in (after_content or ''):\n            errors.append('覆盖后 research.md 缺 skill:research 正文（覆盖内容不对）')\n```\n\nThen exception (system prompt non-empty), reuse normal agent_dir (or a fresh deploy). I'll reuse agent_dir (already deployed). But agent_dir is only valid if normal path succeeded. To be safe, I'll do a fresh deploy into a dedicated dir for the exception phase, OR reuse and guard. Let me do a fresh deploy into a dedicated dir to keep phases independent:\n\nActually, reuse is fine and simpler; but if normal path failed (rc != 0), agent_dir may be empty. Let me do the exception phase with a fresh deploy in its own dir to be robust:\n\n```python\n    # ---------- 异常：system prompt 非空 ----------\n    ex_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_ex_')\n    ex_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_exhome_')\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, ex_dir, ex_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (异常阶段) exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(ex_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('异常阶段 %s.md 未落盘' % name)\n                continue\n            content = read_text(p)\n            fm, body, ferr = parse_frontmatter(content)\n            if ferr:\n                errors.append('异常阶段 %s.md frontmatter 解析失败: %s' % (name, ferr))\n                continue\n            nonblank = count_body_nonblank(body)\n            if nonblank < 1:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 闭合后无非空正文（system prompt 为空）' % name)\n            marker = AGENTS[name]['skill_marker']\n            if marker not in (body or ''):\n                errors.append('%s.md system prompt 缺 %s（wiki 内容未注入）' % (name, marker))\n```\n\nThen go test ./internal/env/... as a compilation/unit check:\n```python\n    # ---------- 结构/编译：go test ./internal/env/... ----------\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'test', '-timeout', '120s', './internal/env/...'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=180)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('go test ./internal/env/... failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n```\n\nThen cleanup temp dirs (best effort), build result, print JSON, exit.\n\nWait — `run` for `go run .` uses cwd=prog_dir. For `go test` uses cwd=repo_root. Fine.\n\nLet me also double-check the `run_deploy` helper signature: `run_deploy(go, prog_dir, target_cwd, agent_dir, home)`. It sets env and runs `[go, 'run', '.', target_cwd]` with cwd=prog_dir.\n\nActually wait — I pass target_cwd as an ARG to `go run . <target>`. Let me confirm `go run . /path` passes `/path` as os.Args[1]. Yes.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: `go run .` with cwd=prog_dir. prog_dir is dot-prefixed under repo_root. Confirmed works.\n\nNow, the `write_deploy_program` writes main.go. Let me include the chdir arg logic.\n\nLet me also think about the `find_repo_root` — I'll copy the robust version from task3/task5.\n\nNow, `discover_agent_names(agents_dir)`:\n```python\ndef discover_agent_names(agents_dir):\n    names = set()\n    if not os.path.isdir(agents_dir):\n        return names\n    for fn in os.listdir(agents_dir):\n        if not fn.endswith('.md'):\n            continue\n        p = os.path.join(agents_dir, fn)\n        content = read_text(p)\n        if content is None:\n            continue\n        fm, _, err = parse_frontmatter(content)\n        if err is None and fm.get('name'):\n            names.add(fm['name'])\n    return names\n```\n\nThis returns the set of frontmatter names (the \"equivalent\" to `{action:\"list\"}`).\n\nNow, let me also make sure the `read_text` returns None on failure and I handle None in parse_frontmatter. parse_frontmatter should handle None content → return error. Let me make parse_frontmatter accept content string; if None, return error.\n\nLet me write everything now.\n\nOne more: `sha256_file` should handle file reading. And `write_file` creates parent dirs.\n\nAlso, for the head-5 check: `read_first_n_lines(path, 5)` returns the first 5 lines joined. I'll implement inline.\n\nLet me write the final script.\n\nI'll also make the docstring concise.\n\nLet me also verify the JSON output requirement: exactly one line JSON to stdout, exit code 0/1. My script only prints via `print(json.dumps(result))`. All debugging to stderr (I won't print debug). Good.\n\nNow, let me write the file using the `write` tool.\n\nActually, I realize there may be an issue with running `go run .` multiple times with different env but same prog_dir: Go caches builds, so it's fast. Good.\n\nLet me also reconsider timeouts: `go run` first time downloads toolchain (~took a few seconds). Subsequent are cached. 240s timeout is generous.\n\nLet me write.\n\nLet me also think: should I verify that the frontmatter `defaultContext` is one of valid values (`fresh`/`fork`)? The task doesn't specify. I'll just check non-empty. Actually, to avoid over-asserting, I'll check presence (key exists) and non-empty. Both covered by `if not fm.get('defaultContext')`.\n\nNow write.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_64qV9XPJp9qYo77KoOk86003","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task9.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"task9 验收测试：注册 think/research/exporter 为 pi 自定义 agent（经 env 职责 3 落盘）。\n\n按 skill:tdd 四要素（前置条件/输入/操作/预期）实现测试方法三类断言，断言真实落盘文件、\n不 mock：用一个临时 Go 程序直接调用真实的 `env.DeployRickCustomizations()`（隔离\nRICK_PI_AGENT_DIR 指向 temp、程序内 chdir 到仓库根使 `.rick/skills` 源可见）。\n\n1. 正常路径：前置=task3/5 完成 + RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR 指向 temp；输入=运行 DeployRickCustomizations；\n   操作=运行 + `test -f agents/{think,research,exporter}.md` + 解析 agents/ 下 frontmatter 的\n   `name` 字段（等价于 pi 真实发现入口 `{action:\"list\"}` 所列 agent 名）；预期=3 文件存在、\n   `head -5 think.md` 含 `name: think`、发现清单 = {think,research,exporter}，且 frontmatter 含\n   name/description/tools/defaultContext + rick-managed: true 标记、tools 对齐 pi 工具名。\n\n2. 边界（幂等 + 覆盖语义）：前置=已注册一次；输入=再次运行；操作=再次运行 + sha256 对比前后；\n   预期=内容不变（幂等）；另预置无 rick-managed: true 的同名文件 → 运行后不被覆盖（仅覆盖有\n   标记的文件）；反向预置含 rick-managed: true 的陈旧文件 → 运行后被覆盖为最新 wiki 正文。\n\n3. 异常（system prompt 非空）：前置=3 文件已写；输入=无；操作=解析 frontmatter 闭合后的正文，\n   等价 `awk '/^---$/{n++} n>=2 && /[^[:space:]]/{print}'` 统计非空行；预期=每文件 ≥1 且含\n   对应 skill wiki 标记（skill:think / skill:research / skill:exporter）。\n\n脚本只读代码 + 跑 go run 临时程序 + go test ./internal/env/...，产物落临时目录，幂等；\n仅向 stdout 输出一行 JSON。\n\"\"\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\n\n\n# 3 个 agent 的期望规格：key = agent 名（也是文件名 {key}.md）。\nAGENTS = {\n    'think': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:think',\n    },\n    'research': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'grep', 'find', 'ls', 'bash', 'web_search', 'fetch_content'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:research',\n    },\n    'exporter': {\n        'tools': ['read', 'write', 'bash'],\n        'skill_marker': 'skill:exporter',\n    },\n}\n\n\n# 临时 Go 程序：真实调用 env.DeployRickCustomizations()。第一个参数为运行期 cwd\n# （chdir 后 workspace.GetRickDir() 才能定位到仓库的 .rick/skills 源目录，与 init-pi\n# 从仓库根运行一致）。\n_DEPLOY_GO = '''package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\ttarget := \".\"\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\ttarget = os.Args[1]\n\t}\n\tif err := os.Chdir(target); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chdir %s failed: %v\\\\n\", target, err)\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\n\t}\n\tif err := env.DeployRickCustomizations(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"deploy failed: %v\\\\n\", err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(\"deploy-ok\")\n}\n'''\n\n\ndef find_repo_root(start_file):\n    \"\"\"定位仓库根目录（绝对路径）。\n\n    优先向上查找 .git 标记；若不存在则回退到脚本相对路径：\n    脚本位于 <root>/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task9.py，向上 5 层即仓库根。\n    \"\"\"\n    d = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(start_file))\n    probe = d\n    while True:\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(probe, '.git')):\n            return probe\n        parent = os.path.dirname(probe)\n        if parent == probe:\n            break\n        probe = parent\n    for _ in range(5):\n        d = os.path.dirname(d)\n    return d\n\n\ndef run(cmd, cwd, timeout=300, env=None):\n    \"\"\"运行子进程，返回 (returncode, stdout, stderr)。\"\"\"\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run(\n            cmd, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env\n        )\n        return p.returncode, p.stdout, p.stderr\n    except FileNotFoundError as e:\n        return 127, '', str(e)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:\n        out = e.stdout or ''\n        err = (e.stderr or '') + '\\n[timeout after %ds]' % timeout\n        return 124, out, err\n\n\ndef tail(text, n=1600):\n    \"\"\"截取文本尾部，用于错误信息（避免刷屏）。\"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return ''\n    return text[-n:]\n\n\ndef read_text(path):\n    \"\"\"读取文本文件内容，失败返回 None。\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            return f.read()\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef write_file(path, content):\n    \"\"\"写文件并自动创建父目录。\"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(content)\n\n\ndef sha256_file(path):\n    \"\"\"计算文件 sha256（十六进制），失败返回 None。\"\"\"\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    try:\n        with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n            for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(65536), b''):\n                h.update(chunk)\n        return h.hexdigest()\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef parse_frontmatter(content):\n    \"\"\"解析 agent 文件，返回 (frontmatter dict, body 字符串, error)。\n\n    frontmatter 由首行 `---` 与随后的第一个 `---` 行闭合；body 为闭合之后全部内容。\n    （skill wiki 正文内部出现的 `---` 水平线属于 body，不影响解析。）\n    \"\"\"\n    if content is None:\n        return None, None, 'file not readable'\n    lines = content.split('\\n')\n    if not lines or lines[0].strip() != '---':\n        return None, None, 'missing opening ---'\n    end = None\n    for i in range(1, len(lines)):\n        if lines[i].strip() == '---':\n            end = i\n            break\n    if end is None:\n        return None, None, 'missing closing ---'\n    fm = {}\n    for ln in lines[1:end]:\n        ln = ln.strip()\n        if not ln or ln.startswith('#'):\n            continue\n        if ':' in ln:\n            k, v = ln.split(':', 1)\n            fm[k.strip()] = v.strip()\n    body = '\\n'.join(lines[end + 1:])\n    return fm, body, None\n\n\ndef count_body_nonblank(body):\n    \"\"\"等价 awk '/^---$/{n++} n>=2 && /[^[:space:]]/{print}' 的非空正文行数。\"\"\"\n    if not body:\n        return 0\n    return sum(1 for ln in body.split('\\n') if ln.strip())\n\n\ndef discover_agent_names(agents_dir):\n    \"\"\"从 agents 目录解析各 .md 的 frontmatter name 字段（等价于 pi {action:\"list\"} 列名）。\"\"\"\n    names = set()\n    if not os.path.isdir(agents_dir):\n        return names\n    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(agents_dir)):\n        if not fn.endswith('.md'):\n            continue\n        content = read_text(os.path.join(agents_dir, fn))\n        fm, _, err = parse_frontmatter(content)\n        if err is None and fm.get('name'):\n            names.add(fm['name'])\n    return names\n\n\ndef write_deploy_program(repo_root):\n    \"\"\"在仓库根下建一个 `.tmp_task9_*` 目录写入临时 Go 程序，返回该目录路径。\n\n    `.` 前缀目录不会被 `go build ./...` / `go test ./...` 拾取；位于模块内方可导入\n    internal 包。运行期 cwd 由程序参数控制（见 _DEPLOY_GO）。\n    \"\"\"\n    tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='.tmp_task9_deploy_', dir=repo_root)\n    write_file(os.path.join(tmpdir, 'main.go'), _DEPLOY_GO)\n    return tmpdir\n\n\ndef run_deploy(go, prog_dir, target_cwd, agent_dir, home):\n    \"\"\"运行临时 Go 程序调用 DeployRickCustomizations，返回 (rc, out, err)。\"\"\"\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env['RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR'] = agent_dir\n    env['HOME'] = home\n    return run([go, 'run', '.', target_cwd], cwd=prog_dir, timeout=240, env=env)\n\n\ndef main():\n    errors = []\n\n    repo_root = find_repo_root(__file__)\n    go = shutil.which('go')\n    if not go:\n        result = {'pass': False, 'errors': ['go toolchain not found in PATH']}\n        print(json.dumps(result))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    prog_dir = write_deploy_program(repo_root)\n\n    # ================= 正常路径 =================\n    agent_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_agent_')\n    home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_home_')\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, agent_dir, home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (正常路径) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        # 3 文件存在 + frontmatter 字段校验。\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('%s.md 未落盘: %s' % (name, p))\n                continue\n            content = read_text(p)\n            fm, body, ferr = parse_frontmatter(content)\n            if ferr:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 解析失败: %s' % (name, ferr))\n                continue\n            if fm.get('name') != name:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter name=%r, want %r' % (name, fm.get('name'), name))\n            got_tools = sorted(t.strip() for t in fm.get('tools', '').split(',') if t.strip())\n            want_tools = sorted(AGENTS[name]['tools'])\n            if got_tools != want_tools:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter tools=%r, want %r' % (name, got_tools, want_tools))\n            if not fm.get('description'):\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺非空 description' % name)\n            if not fm.get('defaultContext'):\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺非空 defaultContext' % name)\n            if fm.get('rick-managed') != 'true':\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 缺 rick-managed: true 标记' % name)\n\n        # `head -5 think.md` 含 `name: think`。\n        think_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', 'think.md')\n        think_content = read_text(think_path)\n        if think_content is None:\n            errors.append('think.md 无法读取（head -5 检查）')\n        else:\n            head5 = '\\n'.join(think_content.split('\\n')[:5])\n            if 'name: think' not in head5:\n                errors.append('head -5 think.md 不含 `name: think`')\n\n        # 真实发现入口（等价：agents/ 下 frontmatter name 字段集合）。\n        discovered = discover_agent_names(os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents'))\n        if discovered != set(AGENTS.keys()):\n            errors.append('agent 发现清单 = %s, want %s'\n                          % (sorted(discovered), sorted(AGENTS.keys())))\n\n        # ================= 边界：幂等 =================\n        before = {}\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if os.path.isfile(p):\n                before[name] = sha256_file(p)\n        rc2, out2, err2 = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, agent_dir, home)\n        if rc2 != 0:\n            errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (幂等重跑) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc2, tail(err2 or out2)))\n        else:\n            changed = []\n            for name, digest in before.items():\n                p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n                if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                    changed.append('%s(file missing)' % name)\n                elif sha256_file(p) != digest:\n                    changed.append(name)\n            if changed:\n                errors.append('幂等重跑后文件内容变化（不幂等）: %s' % ', '.join(changed))\n\n    # ================= 边界：覆盖语义（无标记不覆盖） =================\n    ow_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_ow_')\n    ow_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_owhome_')\n    think_ow = os.path.join(ow_dir, 'agents', 'think.md')\n    user_content = '---\\nname: think\\ndescription: user custom agent\\ntools: read\\n---\\nUSER CUSTOM BODY\\n'\n    write_file(think_ow, user_content)\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, ow_dir, ow_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (覆盖语义-无标记) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        after_content = read_text(think_ow)\n        if after_content != user_content:\n            errors.append('无 rick-managed: true 标记的 think.md 被覆盖（应跳过不覆盖）')\n        for name in ('research', 'exporter'):\n            p = os.path.join(ow_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('覆盖语义（无标记）场景下 %s.md 未落盘' % name)\n\n    # ================= 边界：覆盖语义（有标记才覆盖） =================\n    mk_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_mk_')\n    mk_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_mkhome_')\n    research_mk = os.path.join(mk_dir, 'agents', 'research.md')\n    stale = ('---\\nname: research\\ndescription: stale rick agent\\ntools: read\\n'\n             'defaultContext: fresh\\nrick-managed: true\\n---\\nSTALE BODY\\n')\n    write_file(research_mk, stale)\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, mk_dir, mk_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (覆盖语义-有标记) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        after_content = read_text(research_mk)\n        if after_content == stale:\n            errors.append('含 rick-managed: true 的 research.md 未被覆盖（应覆盖）')\n        elif 'STALE BODY' in (after_content or ''):\n            errors.append('含 rick-managed: true 的 research.md 覆盖后仍含 STALE BODY')\n        elif 'skill:research' not in (after_content or ''):\n            errors.append('覆盖后 research.md 缺 skill:research 正文（覆盖内容不对）')\n\n    # ================= 异常：system prompt 非空 =================\n    ex_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_ex_')\n    ex_home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task9_exhome_')\n    rc, out, err = run_deploy(go, prog_dir, repo_root, ex_dir, ex_home)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations (异常阶段) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(ex_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('异常阶段 %s.md 未落盘' % name)\n                continue\n            content = read_text(p)\n            fm, body, ferr = parse_frontmatter(content)\n            if ferr:\n                errors.append('异常阶段 %s.md frontmatter 解析失败: %s' % (name, ferr))\n                continue\n            if count_body_nonblank(body) < 1:\n                errors.append('%s.md frontmatter 闭合后无非空正文（system prompt 为空）' % name)\n            if AGENTS[name]['skill_marker'] not in (body or ''):\n                errors.append('%s.md system prompt 缺 %s（wiki 内容未注入）'\n                              % (name, AGENTS[name]['skill_marker']))\n\n    # ================= 结构/编译：go test ./internal/env/... =================\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'test', '-timeout', '120s', './internal/env/...'],\n                       cwd=repo_root, timeout=180)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('go test ./internal/env/... failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n\n    # 清理临时 Go 程序目录（agent_dir/home 等系统临时目录由 tempfile 管理）。\n    shutil.rmtree(prog_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n    result = {\n        'pass': len(errors) == 0,\n        'errors': errors,\n    }\n\n    # CRITICAL: 仅此一行输出到 stdout\n    print(json.dumps(result))\n\n    sys.exit(0 if result['pass'] else 1)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":252,"output":7769,"cacheRead":82816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3424,"totalTokens":90837,"cost":{"input":0.00010962000000000001,"output":0.00675903,"cacheRead":0.000300208,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007168858}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786908125659,"responseId":"67b2c1ed-a929-4d30-b123-e626fe1783ac","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_64qV9XPJp9qYo77KoOk86003","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 13636 bytes to /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task9.py"}],"is